opennyai_summary.decision:
9. After bestowing my anxious consideration to the facts, the materials placed on record, and the rival 2024:KER:75554 BAIL APPL. NO. 7093 OF 2024 submissions made across the Bar, and taking note of the principles laid down by the Hon'ble Supreme Court in the afore-cited decision, and on considering the fact that the marital relationship between the first petitioner and the de facto complainant is strained and there are disputes pending between them, and further that there is a delay in registering the FIR, I am satisfied and convinced that the petitioners have made out valid grounds to invoke the discretionary jurisdiction of this Court under Section 482 of the BNS.
Hence,
I am inclined to allow the application, but subject to stringent conditions.
In the result, the application is allowed subject to the following conditions:
(i) The petitioners are directed to surrender before the Investigating Officer within 10 days from today;
(ii) In the event of the petitioners' arrest, the Investigating Officer shall release the petitioners on bail on them executing a bond for 2024:KER:75554 BAIL APPL. NO.
7093 OF 2024 Rs.50,000/- (Rupees fifty thousand only) each with two solvent sureties for the like amount each;
(iii) The petitioners shall appear before the Investigating Officer between 9 a.m and 11 a.m on Mondays and Fridays for two weeks from the date of their release.
They shall then appear before the Investigating Officer, as and when directed;

